==Battleground==
*Infinite [[B.B.Bunny|B.B.Bunnies]] spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
*6 [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
*2 [[St. Pigge the 2nd]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 60~66.67 seconds<sup>1,800f~2,000f</sup>.
*3 [[One Horn]]s spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.
*1 [[Bore]] spawns after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>.
*1 [[J.K. Bun Bun]] spawns after 106.67 seconds<sup>3,200f</sup>.
*1 [[Dark Emperor Nyandam]] spawns as the boss after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.

==Strategy==

Anti-red units make this stage rather trivial, such as [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Apple Cat]] or [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Sushi Cat]], because the stage is made up of only red enemies.

Since the Bore only spawns after 60 seconds, it is possible (and quite easy) to clear the stage before it even spawns using rushers like [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] and [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|A. Bahamut]]. If you don't have any fast rushers, this stage only becomes a bit harder because the Bore can be killed before the J.K. Bun Bun spawns.

One thing to avoid is trying to stall the Bore, as doing so can cause the J.K. Bun Bun to push along with the Bore and destroy your base.

